  "reason": "RNA-only multiprofile models are currently strongest, especially scvi_n200 with avgpool/transformer around 0.65 validation accuracy, while image-only single-profile models are weak (ResNet50 0.208, ViT 0.227). The key uncertainty is whether multiprofile aggregation can make the image modality useful before investing in many multimodal fusion configurations. config_014 directly extends the best single-profile image baseline by testing imagenet_vit_l with multiprofile and simple avgpool aggregation, isolating the effect of profile setting/aggregation for image representations. This is the best use of the next budget because it is simpler than multimodal testing, reduces uncertainty about whether image features can contribute at all, and will inform whether multimodal fusion experiments are worth pursuing."
}

